    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Corbin Carroll**, who commands the highest efficiency score of 74.78. Despite the threat of a quick catcher, the matchup against Landen Roupp is prime for a breakout, with a 6% boost from platoon splits and an optimal #2 spot in the order driving his elite status. While **Austin Riley** carries a slightly lower score at 63.51, he represents an opportunistic play against Garrett, B, whose ballooning 9.71 xERA provides the highest upside for RBI and HR production on the board. **Josh Naylor** similarly benefits from the soft arm of Anthony Kay, utilizing a 19% SP skill advantage to secure a strong 64.71 rating. **Brice Turang** remains a tactical necessity; his 56.74 score is bolstered by a 4% efficiency boost specifically tied to the slow delivery of Ben Brown, maximizing his elite stolen base potential\u2014the lifeblood of our roster strategy.\n\nManaging our bench proved difficult, as **Vinnie Pasquantino** sat on the precipice of a start with a 43.03 score. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Mickey Moniak**, whose 14% park-factor advantage in his current venue outweighed the downside of facing Tyler Alexander. However, we must remain vigilant regarding the 36%\u201345% rain risk hovering over the games involving **Travis Bazzana**, **Kyle Karros**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Zach McKinstry**. Should these contests face significant delays, the bench depth provided by **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Tyler Soderstrom** will be critical for late-cycle adjustments. We are also monitoring the status of **Jose Caballero**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while keeping an eye on the defensive flexibility of **Max Muncy**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Henry Bolte** to ensure we don't bleed plate appearances if lineups shift post-publication.",
